From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vendor crash-context 0.7.0 for riscv64 getcontext() support

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 getcontext support needs a newer transitive dependency crash-handler's own Cargo.toml pins out of semver range]

fbuild's running-process/zccache dependencies pull in crash-handler,
which depends on `crash-context = "0.6"`. crash-context 0.6.3 (the
only version satisfying that range before this patch) has no riscv64
branch anywhere in its getcontext()/ucontext_t/fpregset_t cfg-if
chains, so the riscv64 build fails with "cannot find type `ucontext_t`
in module `super`" compiling that crate directly.

crash-context 0.7.0 (EmbarkStudios/crash-handling#102) added real
riscv64 support (ucontext_t/mcontext_t layout plus a hand-written
crash_context_getcontext asm routine), but it can't just be bumped to:
crash-handler 0.6.3 AND 0.7.0 (both locked in this workspace, pulled in
by zccache and running-process-probe respectively) each pin
`crash-context = "0.6"`, a caret requirement that rejects 0.7.0/0.8.0
outright, and neither of those crates is ours to patch (both are
external git dependencies, not fbuild workspace members).

Vendors the complete, unmodified crash-context 0.7.0 release (from its
own published .crate tarball) under vendor/crash-context/, with only
its Cargo.toml version string turned back to "0.6.3" so it keeps
satisfying every "crash-context = 0.6" requirement in the graph, and
wires it in via [patch.crates-io] in the top-level Cargo.toml -- a
standard Cargo mechanism for substituting a transitive dependency's
source without needing to fork everything above it in the dependency
graph. No hand-written code: the riscv64 getcontext asm, ucontext_t/
mcontext_t/fpregset_t layout and everything else come straight from
crash-context's own tested, released 0.7.0 source.

Validated: `cargo check` on the vendored crate standalone (both the
default host target and a cross-check against the installed
riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu rust-std component -- the latter failed in
this sandbox on an unrelated "can't find crate for `core`" sysroot
issue affecting every crate including libc, not anything in this
patch, so riscv64 codegen itself is unverified locally) and the whole
patch applying cleanly against a fresh v2.5.21 checkout.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index a7c341b..f4514cf 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -205,3 +205,14 @@ debug = "line-tables-only"
 [profile.dev.package."*"]
 opt-level = 3
 debug = false
+
+[patch.crates-io]
+# crash-context 0.6.3 (the version crash-handler 0.6/0.7 both require) has
+# no riscv64 getcontext() implementation at all -- `target_arch = "riscv64"`
+# falls through its cfg-if chain with no branch, leaving ucontext_t/
+# fpregset_t undefined. Vendor the real upstream 0.7.0 release (which added
+# riscv64 support, EmbarkStudios/crash-handling#102) with its version string
+# alone turned back to "0.6.3" so it still satisfies crash-handler's "0.6"
+# requirement; everything else, including the riscv64 getcontext asm, is
+# unmodified upstream code.
+crash-context = { path = "vendor/crash-context" }
